<!-- @after Common Misconceptions :: check -->
**Which thread runs it?** Decide before opening each answer.

<details><summary><code>Handler(Looper.getMainLooper()).post { … }</code> called from a background thread.</summary>

The main thread. A Handler runs work on its Looper's thread, not the caller's.
</details>

<details><summary>Parsing a 10 MB JSON file posted to a <code>HandlerThread</code> that also handles camera frames.</summary>

That one thread: and while it parses, no camera frame is handled. Run CPU-heavy work on `Dispatchers.Default` or a pool.
</details>

<details><summary>A coroutine resumes on <code>Dispatchers.Main</code>.</summary>

The main thread. The regular Main dispatcher posts through its Handler; `Dispatchers.Main.immediate` can avoid an extra dispatch when already on the matching Looper.
</details>
